---
// About section with original purple/orange gradient design
---

<section id="about" class="pt-20 pb-20 bio-block section-layer">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="bio-container rounded-lg p-8">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8 text-center text-pink-200">About</h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto items-start">
      <!-- What Drives Me -->
      <div class="bio-card fade-in-on-scroll">
        <svg class="bio-card-border" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <defs>
            <linearGradient id="borderGradient1" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="100%">
              <stop offset="0%" style="stop-color:rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6);stop-opacity:1">
                <animate attributeName="stop-color" 
                  values="rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6);rgba(255, 150, 100, 0.75);rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6)" 
                  dur="8s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
              </stop>
              <stop offset="50%" style="stop-color:rgba(255, 150, 100, 0.75);stop-opacity:1">
                <animate attributeName="stop-color" 
                  values="rgba(255, 150, 100, 0.75);rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6);rgba(255, 150, 100, 0.75)" 
                  dur="8s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
              </stop>
              <stop offset="100%" style="stop-color:rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6);stop-opacity:1">
                <animate attributeName="stop-color" 
                  values="rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6);rgba(255, 150, 100, 0.75);rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6)" 
                  dur="8s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
              </stop>
            </linearGradient>
          </defs>
          <rect x="1" y="1" rx="12" ry="12" stroke="url(#borderGradient1)" stroke-width="2" 
                fill="none" stroke-dasharray="8 6" stroke-linecap="round">
            <animate attributeName="stroke-dashoffset" from="28" to="0" dur="16s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
          </rect>
        </svg>
        <div class="bio-card-content">
          <p class="text-white leading-relaxed">
          Hardware fascinates me, especially in unusual target environments. <br /> <br />I'm privileged to have designed and engineered systems that operate in many contexts, including inside <span class="highlight-text">the human body</span>, <span class="highlight-text">30,000 feet in the air</span>, and across millions of phones, computers, and servers.
          <br /><br />
          The perfect pairing of software and hardware is bliss.
        </p>

        <details class="additional-info">
          <summary class="text-orange-300 cursor-pointer hover:text-orange-200 text-sm font-semibold mt-4">
            <span class="expand-icon">+</span> Philosophy, stack & practice
          </summary>
          <div class="details-content">
            <div class="mt-3 text-white/90 text-sm space-y-4 leading-relaxed">
              <p><strong class="text-pink-200">Design Philosophy:</strong> Start from first principles. Bias toward simplicity and correctness. Less is more but don't be cheap.</p>
              <p><strong class="text-pink-200">Stack Preference:</strong> Whatever fits the problem. Most at home in C/C++, Python, and Linux.</p>
              <p class="mb-1"><strong class="text-pink-200">Practice:</strong></p>
              <ul class="details-bullets">
                <li><span class="highlight-text">Look around corners.</span></li>
                <li>Pre-empt pain.</li>
                <li>Identify investment vs. sunk cost.</li>
                <li>Write the docs you wish you had.</li>
                <li><span class="highlight-text">Get it done.</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Currently -->
      <div class="bio-card fade-in-on-scroll">
        <svg class="bio-card-border" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <defs>
            <linearGradient id="borderGradient2" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="100%">
              <stop offset="0%" style="stop-color:rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6);stop-opacity:1">
                <animate attributeName="stop-color" 
                  values="rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6);rgba(255, 150, 100, 0.75);rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6)" 
                  dur="8s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="2s"/>
              </stop>
              <stop offset="50%" style="stop-color:rgba(255, 150, 100, 0.75);stop-opacity:1">
                <animate attributeName="stop-color" 
                  values="rgba(255, 150, 100, 0.75);rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6);rgba(255, 150, 100, 0.75)" 
                  dur="8s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="2s"/>
              </stop>
              <stop offset="100%" style="stop-color:rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6);stop-opacity:1">
                <animate attributeName="stop-color" 
                  values="rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6);rgba(255, 150, 100, 0.75);rgba(140, 120, 160, 0.6)" 
                  dur="8s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="2s"/>
              </stop>
            </linearGradient>
          </defs>
          <rect x="1" y="1" rx="12" ry="12" stroke="url(#borderGradient2)" stroke-width="2" 
                fill="none" stroke-dasharray="8 6" stroke-linecap="round">
            <animate attributeName="stroke-dashoffset" from="28" to="0" dur="16s" repeatCount="indefinite" begin="2s"/>
          </rect>
        </svg>
        <div class="bio-card-content">
          <p class="text-white leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Currently focusing on
          </p>
          <ul class="details-bullets">
            <li>Intelligent systems under real-world constraints</li>
            <li>Probabilistic reasoning and adaptive architectures</li>
            <li>Prototyping physical devices and interfaces on my CNC machine</li>
            <li>Designing <span class="highlight-text">systems that last</span>: anticipating failure modes and how systems evolve over time</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-white leading-relaxed mt-6 mb-4">
          I’ve also been studying how models and representations shape system behavior especially when abstractions begin to influence reality more than the underlying system itself. A recent example I’ve been thinking about: <span class="highlight-text">sneckdowns</span>.
          </p>
          <p class="text-white leading-relaxed mt-4 mb-2">
            Recent reads:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-white/80 space-y-1 text-sm">
            <li>Gigantic Cinema: A Weather Anthology</li>
            <li>Thinking In Systems - Donella Meadows</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .bio-block {
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #5a5a5a 0%, #5a5a5a 5%, #625870 30%, #6b5d77 60%, rgba(107, 93, 119, 0.8) 100%);
  }

  .bio-container {
    background-color: rgba(80, 70, 90, 0.5);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
  }

  .bio-card {
    position: relative;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .bio-card-border {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .bio-card-border rect {
    width: calc(100% - 2px);
    height: calc(100% - 2px);
  }

  .bio-card-content {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .bio-card:hover {
    background-color: rgba(100, 90, 110, 0.35);
    transform: scale(1.01);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4), 0 0 20px rgba(255, 160, 122, 0.15);
  }

  .bio-card:hover .bio-card-border rect {
    stroke-width: 3;
  }

  .bio-card p {
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .additional-info {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px dashed rgba(190, 156, 212, 0.3);
  }

  .additional-info summary {
    list-style: none;
    user-select: none;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .additional-info summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .additional-info[open] summary {
    color: #ffa07a;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .additional-info summary:hover {
    transform: translateX(2px);
  }

  .expand-icon {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 1.2rem;
    text-align: center;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 1.2em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .details-content {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 0fr;
    transition: grid-template-rows 0.5s ease-out;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .additional-info[open] .details-content {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }

  .details-content > * {
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .details-bullets {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .details-bullets li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .details-bullets li::before {
    content: "▸";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: #ffa07a;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  .highlight-text {
    color: #ff9966;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255, 160, 122, 0.3);
  }
</style>

<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const detailsElements = document.querySelectorAll('.additional-info');
    
    detailsElements.forEach(details => {
      details.addEventListener('toggle', () => {
        const icon = details.querySelector('.expand-icon');
        if (icon) {
          icon.textContent = details.open ? '−' : '+';
        }
      });
    });
  });
</script>
